    (0, None, '\'This is simply some kind of real holiday!\' "Prazdnik kakoy-to" is "some kind of holiday": the -to on "kakoy" makes it vague. "Prazdnik" is the root of "prazdnichny tort", the celebration cake. Barinov is very pleased with himself.'),
    (1, None, '\'Chef, why are you smiling so joyfully?\' "Ulybaetes" is "you are smiling", polite form, with -s on the end. "Radostno", "joyfully", comes from "radost", "joy", the family of Vika\'s "rada", "glad". Lyova is polite and puzzled.'),
